# BEAM: the source amplitude profile -- UNIFORM (default) vs GAUSSIAN with 1-unit waists -- seen in the far-field
# INT peak of the manual's Cassegrain (cmdref: Diffraction).  NONE first.  The Gaussian beam re-propagates
# (BEAM clears the propagate state) and the peak moves from 8.877e6 to 2.920e6 and the summed intensity
# from 3.313e8 to 2.139e8: the Gaussian is normalized to the uniform beam's flux with the tail the aperture
# truncates LOST (Dave 2026-10-19, PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (y); before, S = sqrt(Flux) at every ray put the
# peak at 6.884e8).  Five figures (rule 2); ifx and gfortran agree to 8.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
none
int 5
beam
gauss
1
1
int 5
beam
uniform
# EXPECT: Peak intensity= 8\.8773143D\+06[\s\S]*?Enter x beam waist radius: \[1\.00000\]: 1\s+Enter y beam waist radius: \[1\.00000\]: 1[\s\S]*?Peak intensity= 2\.9204\d*D\+06; Peak occurs at i=\s+129, j=\s+129\s+Sum of intensity= 2\.1394\d*D\+08
# EXPECT-NOT: Unknown beam type
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
